
[38;5;231m⏺[39m The implementation plan is at [38;5;153mdocs/hyperpowers/plans/2026-10-02-deploys-page.md[39m. I haven't started implementing, and I
  haven't committed the plan either.

  [1mWhat it does:[0m
  - [1mTask 1: the page itself[0m ([38;5;153msrc/pages/deploys.js[39m plus its tests). It uses the same query handling as the Services page,
    but builds the markup from the bundled [38;5;153m#kit[39m components instead of copying the Services HTML. The kit already has
    everything the spec asks for: page header, filter bar, dropdown, sortable table, colored chips and an empty-state
    message. The task has 12 tests covering the filter, both sorts, the chips, the durations, both empty states, the
    fallback for unknown query values, and escaping.
  - [1mTask 2: hooking it up.[0m This adds the [38;5;153m/deploys[39m route, the nav link right after Services, and server tests: the route,
    the nav position, and the 503 page for both a missing and a corrupt [38;5;153mdeploys.json[39m. It also mentions the page in the
    README.

  [1mSomething the spec doesn't mention:[0m the test suites that click through every nav link run against
  [38;5;153mtest/e2e/fixtures/empty/[39m and [38;5;153msingle/[39m, which have no [38;5;153mdeploys.json[39m. Adding the nav link alone makes them fail with a
  503, so Task 2 adds both fixture files and includes a step showing that failure first.

  [1mDecisions I made where the spec is open[0m (listed at the end of the plan, so you can overrule them):
  - With "All environments" selected and no deploys at all, the page says "No deploys", since there's no environment to
    name.
  - With no valid [38;5;153mdir[39m, Started sorts newest first and Service sorts A–Z.
  - Times use the existing [38;5;153mformatTimestamp[39m helper, so they show as "2026-10-01 09:05 UTC" rather than raw ISO strings.
  - Deploys longer than an hour stay in minutes, e.g. "75m 0s".

  [1mChecks:[0m
  - I applied the plan's code to a throwaway copy of the repo in [38;5;153m/tmp[39m and ran the full suite: all 395 tests passed. That
    copy is deleted, so your working tree only has the new plan file.
  - Codex isn't installed here, so the extra Codex review of the plan was skipped. That's recorded in the ungated-review
    log; neither task is marked low-risk, so nothing loses its per-task review because of it.

  Once you've read it and are happy, tell me to go ahead and I'll run it task by task, with a fresh subagent and a
  review for each task.

